# Pattern: A gate prints a verdict and a list of offending names, and somebody quotes it -- in a brief, a report, a handover note. The quote carries the numbers and the names and not the one fact that makes them checkable: WHICH TREE they were measured on. Later a second reader runs the same gate on the tree they have and gets a different answer. There is now no way to tell the two possibilities apart from the artefact alone: the claim was wrong, or the claim was right about a tree this reader does not have -- work that has not landed, a branch nobody can fetch, a base that has since moved. The second is not hypothetical and it is not rare, because parallel lanes quote each other's measurements constantly and land at different times. Resolving it without the stamp is expensive: the reader must search every reachable reference for the work the claim depends on, and then reconstruct it locally to test the claim at all.
